{"stage":"premise-check","note":"All premises in the hardening brief verified against the cited file and line before implementing. Four already-done fixes confirmed present at pipeline.mjs:362 (dup-id), :589 (array picks), :375 (rewrite_of), :795 (pair gating). validateCurator text-diff confirmed at :989. No merge stage confirmed. flags_for_reviewer confirmed a string array at curator brief line 73. Substring flag matching confirmed at :970. RUBRIC R13 capitals confirmed. hedge_counts per option confirmed.","ok":true}
{"stage":"premise-CORRECTION","severity":"high","claim":"'the actual difference was straight single quotes becoming curly double quotes'","observed":"WRONG, and my own 2026-09-19 report was wrong the same way. Character census: source candidate stem = U+0027 x3 only. Curator staging = U+0022 x8 + U+0027 x8. Render output = U+0027 x16. There are ZERO typographic characters (U+2018/2019/201C/201D) in any of the three files. The drift was pure ASCII: straight SINGLE outer quotes became straight DOUBLE outer quotes.","consequence":"the Task 3 lint as specified (reject U+2018/2019/201C/201D) would NOT have caught the defect that actually occurred. Added CANON-outer, which does: it flags a single-quoted outer span and ignores apostrophes. Catches 13 of 17 real P1 candidates.","second_consequence":"by the canonical rule in the brief itself ('double for outer, single when nested') the CURATOR was right and the GENERATOR was wrong. The generator brief now states the rule.","ok":true}
{"stage":"premise-CORRECTION","severity":"medium","claim":"Task 6: 'detect NOT/EXCEPT in a stem case-insensitively and fail when uncapitalised'","observed":"Too broad as written. Implemented literally it fires on candidate d01, whose stem reads 'comparable to not knowing whether something costs one dollar or a trillion' — incidental prose, not a negation stem. Also would fire on 'cannot', 'note that'.","action":"narrowed to a negation TASK construction: an interrogative head (which/what/all/each/every) followed within 80 chars by not/except. d01 now clean; 'Which of the following is not true?' still flagged. Verified both directions.","ok":true}
{"stage":"decision","topic":"rewrite id convention","picked":"r-suffix, both objects retained (a01 and a01r)","rejected":"resolving a rewrite under the original's id and overwriting it (was pipeline.mjs:981-983)","why":"runs/ is an audit trail; overwriting destroys the before/after that produced the finding 'all 6 rewrites clear the joint length gate, a03r rescued from 1.15 to 1.06'. measure already admits rewrite_of.","applied_everywhere":["merge promotes rewrites to <id>r","eligibleIds names the rewrite, not the superseded original","validateCurator resolves selected ids against candidates.json only"],"ok":true}
{"stage":"decision","topic":"sharding","picked":"DROP as the default generation strategy","why":"lost the A/B on every measured axis. The only things it buys are mechanical enforcement of the analyst's attempts budget and a smaller blast radius per failed call; both are obtainable by passing the attempts budget into a whole-section prompt and running 2-3 calls.","action":"recorded, but the shard stage is NOT removed in this pass: it is not among the six tasks, the evidence is one section, and deleting it would orphan existing run artifacts.","ok":true}
{"stage":"task1","action":"render stage added; curator no longer writes staging/<section>.md; stem/option/explanation diff DELETED from validateCurator as unnecessary rather than fixed","verified":"render output is byte-identical to candidates.json text (16 apostrophes, source verbatim)","ok":true}
{"stage":"task2","action":"merge stage added: reads candidates/*.json, splits trailing {note} into generator-notes.json, assigns ids from (shard,index), dies on collision, promotes rewrites to <id>r, writes id-provenance.json","verified":"reproduces exactly the 17 candidates and ids built by hand in P1","also":"flags_for_reviewer schema changed to [{id,note}]; validate matches ids exactly, no substring search; short-form ids deliberately not accepted (opus/c01r and sonnet/c01r both shorten to c01r)","ok":true}
{"stage":"task3","action":"canonical ASCII lint: CANON-quote (typographic), CANON-outer (single-quoted outer span), CANON-emph (underscore emphasis). render applies typographic quotes only under --smart-quotes, deterministically, never a model.","ok":true}
{"stage":"task4","action":"emphasis_counts measured per option beside length and hedge_counts; gated with R9's rule shape — key must not be unique max or unique min. Emphasis NOT banned.","ok":true}
{"stage":"task5","action":"validate split into FAIL and WARN; exit code driven by FAIL only. On the real P1 data this turns 3 blocking cosmetic alarms into 0 FAIL / 28 WARN.","ok":true}
{"stage":"task6","action":"R13 negation-capitals gate added to tier 2, plus a flag cross-check in lint. Script owns the measurement; the candidate's negation flag is checked against it in both directions.","ok":true}
{"stage":"selftest","observed":"48 assertions (was 40), green, and now IDEMPOTENT — it previously left fixtures behind, and a stale curator.json made the suite fail on its own second run. selftest now clears runs/_selftest at start.","bug_found_and_fixed":"the first version of the new render assertion wrote to staging/forecasting-timelines.md, the REAL path, clobbering the live staged section. Restored from git; the test now snapshots and restores.","ok":true}

